==Strategy==
It is recommended to get extra money from the first peons with cats like [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. You can cheese this stage with Unit Attack UP and money-related [[Cat Combo|Combos]], Can Can Cat (Money Up and Move Speed Up Talents) and rusher-type units, such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], or [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]]. If you don't wish to cheese it, You may also want to use [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shields]] and/or [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Wave-immune units]]. Try not to take too much time against Cosmic Cyclone, or else the Midnite Ds, Lutrinae Gokurakkos and Bore Jrs. can be annoying.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Dioramos (Uber Rare Cat)|Ascendant Dioramos]]: Dioramos can Slow and Knockback this stage's Cosmic Cyclone and Gokurakko, vastly reducing their pushing power. Not only that, he is extremely bulky and won't be juggled by Bore Jr.'s waves.
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Luna has a dual purpose on this stage. First of all, she can Freeze Cosmic Cyclone, reducing its pushing power and allowing your other units to attack it more easily. Secondly, with her Wave Blocker ability, she can nullify Bore Jr.'s Wave Attacks.

==Trivia==
*The Japanese names of [[Furious Field]] and Mirage Meadow are puns. Both have the word ''kyozō'' in their names, but written with different kanji to form different meanings. Furious Field spells ''kyozō'' as 巨象, meaning "[[Le'mammoth|giant elephant]]", whereas Mirage Meadow uses 虚像, referring to a [[wikipedia:Virtual image|virtual image]].

